# Ignore list for the API image. The build context is the repository root
# (docker build -f api/Dockerfile .), so every pattern is relative to the root.
# The image needs api/Cargo.toml, api/Cargo.lock, api/src and db/migrations and
# nothing else.
#
# Docker reads the ignore file from the context root, or from
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile. This is the second form, which
# is the one that actually applies to `docker build -f api/Dockerfile .`; a plain
# api/.dockerignore would be ignored entirely for a root-context build.

# other services
analytics/
billing/
tools/
web/
infra/
docs/
scripts/

# build output and local state
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/.next/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# version control, CI metadata and editors
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
*.log

# local secrets: never bake these into an image
.env
.env.*

# repository documentation and local orchestration
*.md
LICENSE
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
